The second launcher attempt found the existing web/socket/worker/scheduler and
left them running, but its Windows HTTP health probe could not reach the named
origin. This hostname is resolved in WSL and in the browser's localhost handling;
the Windows-native resolver is a different context. The health gate now runs
inside WSL using the same named origin, requiring HTTP 200 and JSON pong. The
launcher does not change the Windows hosts file or substitute an unrelated site.
